            <ArticleTitle>Controlled trial of homoeopathic treatment of osteoarthritis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a double-blind, placebo-controlled crossover study to compare the homoeopathic remedy Rhus tox. 6X with fenoprofen in osteoarthritis of the hip and knee, fenoprofen was shown to have beneficial analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects which differed significantly from those of placebo. The effects of Rhus tox. 6X and placebo did not differ significantly. Patient preference was for fenoprofen. Side-effects were not severe but were seen more frequently with fenoprofen. Similar results were seen in all patients regardless of whether they had been referred to and assessed by a homoeopathic physician or a rheumatologist.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
